  "analysis": "# Analysis — 1998-06-14 — Bremen, Germany, Stadthalle\n*Claude claude-sonnet-4-6 — 2026-06-17*\n\n## Verdict: 8 recordings — 6 families — result needs review — 2 LBs missing from disk, and two taper-claimed same-recording pairs (LB-02261/LB-10954, LB-06499/LB-15221) were kept separate by tapematch\n\n| LB | Rating | Timing | Source | Family | Notes |\n|----|--------|--------|--------|--------|-------|\n| LB-02261 | A- | 60min+49min | (a bittorrent from 4/07 is same recording with similar wav and spectral views except… | 6 | |\n| LB-05505 | A | 60min+47min | net taper I, lineage, OKMII -> portable Sony DATrecorder - clone ->(digital transfer)… | 5 | |\n| LB-06494 | A | 60min+47min | ssrc; net taper I, OKMII -> portable Sony DATrecorder - clone ->(digital transfer)… | 5 | |\n| LB-06499 | A | 60min+48min | net taper F, OKMII -> portable Sony DATrecorder - clone ->(digital transfer) m-audio… | 1 | |\n| LB-07589 | — | — | — | — | not found on disk |\n| LB-10639 | B+ | 71min+38min | version \"e\", Alternative recording to LB-2261 & 'NTI' & 'NTF'., Trade cd-rs from many… | 2 | |\n| LB-10954 | A- | 76min+78min | BOOTLEG: you will remember my name; Label:, The Godfather Records, Catalog number: G.R.… | 3 | inflated 44.4%; medium confidence merge |\n| LB-11522 | A- | 60min+49min | version \"g\", unknown source; sorry, no more informations | 3 | medium confidence merge |\n| LB-14010 | — | — | — | — | not found on disk |\n| LB-15221 | A |  | ds archive 48, OKMII>Sony DAT>clone, to me>file cloned in Microtrack using, a Tascam Dat… | 4 | |\n\n### Coverage gap — 2 of 10 DB entries not found on disk\nLB-07589 and LB-14010 have info-file commentary in the bundle but no audio on disk, so tapematch could not include them in this run. Both report explicit comparisons against the analyzed sources (LB-07589: \"different recording than LB-2261 and NTI LB-6494... NTF LB-6499 are very close, and LB-2261 is harsher\"; LB-14010: \"in 6-way comparison this is a different recording... has a fuller sound than LB-2261; not as warm or full as ltb LB-7589, nti LB-6494, and ntf LB-6499\"). Worth re-running once those files are located, since they add two more apparently-distinct sources to the picture.\n\n### LB-02261 / LB-10954 — commentary claims same recording, tapematch disagrees\nLB-10954's info file states \"same recording as LB-2261 based on same clapping wavs at beginning of d1t1; this has been sound processed to reduce clapping and some in between song crowd noise has been removed.\" tapematch instead merges LB-10954 with LB-11522 (corr 0.789, medium confidence) and keeps LB-02261 fully isolated (`[DISTINCT SOURCE]`, best cross-family corr 0.006 — near zero against everything, including LB-10954). LB-11522's own note (\"not a close eac match on d1t1 to LB-2261\") is at least consistent with LB-02261 being the odd one out. The clapping-based claim and the near-zero correlation are hard to reconcile from text alone — this pairing needs a manual listen.\n\n### LB-06499 / LB-15221 — commentary claims same recording, tapematch disagrees\nLB-15221's info file states \"same recording as LB-6499 based on same clapping wavs at end of t1... at 48k with higher levels,\" but tapematch keeps LB-15221 (Family 4) and LB-06499 (Family 1) fully separate — both show essentially zero correlation to every other source in the matrix. As with the LB-02261/LB-10954 case, the taper's clapping-match claim conflicts with the measured correlation; flag for manual review rather than accepting either call outright.\n\n### LB-10954 / LB-11522 — medium-confidence merge\nFamily 3 (corr 0.789) is plausible given LB-10954's own note that audience noise was processed/removed from the official Godfather Records release, which would suppress correlation against a same-source raw audience tape. No independent taper note explicitly links LB-10954 to LB-11522, so this rests on tapematch's correlation alone — reasonable but not as strongly corroborated as the Family 5 merge below.\n\n### LB-05505 / LB-06494 — high-confidence merge, corroborated by taper notes\nFamily 5 (corr 0.943) is confirmed by LB-06494's own page: \"same recording as LB-5505 based on same clapping wavs at end of d1t3.\" Correct.\n\n### LB-02261 — confirmed distinct source\n`[DISTINCT SOURCE]` flag (-500 ppm, best cross-family corr 0.006) is consistent with it being a different, harsher-sounding recording per multiple other tapers' comparative notes (LB-07589, LB-10639, LB-14010 all describe LB-02261 as audibly different/harsher in multi-way comparisons).\n"
